{"name":"Boiling Mud","hex":"#a59c9b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boiling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of boil"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process of changing the state of a substance from liquid to gas by heating it to its boiling point.","The cooking (of food) or cleaning (of an object) by immersing it in liquid (usually water) that is boiling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boiling"},{"term":"mud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mednyj Aleut."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of water and soil or fine grained sediment.","A plaster-like mixture used to texture or smooth drywall."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mud"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boiling","blocks":[{"text":"Boiling or ebullition is the rapid phase transition from liquid to gas or vapour; the reverse of boiling is condensation. Boiling occurs when a liquid is heated to its boiling point, so that the vapour pressure of the liquid is equal to the pressure exerted on the liquid by the surrounding atmosphere. Boiling and evaporation are the two main forms of liquid vapourization."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Boilingkettle.jpg/330px-Boilingkettle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling"},{"title":"Mud","blocks":[{"text":"Mud is loam, silt, or clay mixed with water. Mud is usually formed after rainfall or near water sources. Ancient mud deposits hardened over geological time to form sedimentary rock such as shale or mudstone. When geological deposits of mud are formed in estuaries, the resultant layers are termed bay muds. Mud has also been used for centuries as a construction resource, mostly for houses, and also as a binder. An Old English word for it was fen, now in most dialects referring to a type of wetland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg/330px-2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boiling pasta","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Pasta_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Gamo_Mud_Volcano_3.jpg/500px-Gamo_Mud_Volcano_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Gamo_Mud_Volcano_3.jpg/1280px-Gamo_Mud_Volcano_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Gamo_Mud_Volcano_3.jpg/500px-Gamo_Mud_Volcano_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gamo mud volcano in Tokamachi, Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGamo_Mud_Volcano_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Punjabi_Home.JPG/500px-Punjabi_Home.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Punjabi_Home.JPG/1280px-Punjabi_